{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k2-reviewer-fable-50","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:307d8fd920b1e2360c2d","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The declared independent-unit column is chamber_id, and the data file contains exactly 24 rows with 24 distinct chamber_id values (CH01 through CH24), so no independent unit contributes more than one row to the analysis.","observed_value":{"n_rows":24,"n_unique_chamber_id":24,"duplicates":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: chamber_id"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"chamber_id,diet,day60_mass_g\nCH01,algal_oil,13.4"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"CH24,baseline,11.0"}]},{"description":"The workflow actively enforces one row per independent unit: read_chambers raises a ValueError if any chamber_id appears on more than one row, so a repeated-unit entry could not silently reach the test.","observed_value":"duplicate chamber_id rows would abort the analysis","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":27,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"tags = [row[\"chamber_id\"] for row in rows]\n    if len(set(tags)) != len(tags):\n        raise ValueError(\"each chamber_id must appear on exactly one row\")"}]},{"description":"Each row enters the row-independent procedure (Fisher's exact test) exactly once: summarise partitions each diet arm's rows into graded (mass >= 12.0 g) and missed counts, and the four cell counts a, b, c, d are passed to fisher_exact once. The graded and missed cells are disjoint by construction, so no unit is double-counted.","observed_value":{"table":[[9,3],[3,9]],"n_total":24},"source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":38,"end_line":39,"quoted_text":"graded = sum(1 for mass in masses if mass >= TARGET_MASS_G)\n    return graded, len(masses) - graded, sum(masses) / len(masses)"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":96,"end_line":96,"quoted_text":"pvalue = float(fisher_exact([[a, b], [c, d]], alternative=\"two-sided\")[1])"}]},{"description":"Independent recomputation from the raw CSV reproduces every number in the selected result: 9 of 12 algal_oil rows and 3 of 12 baseline rows have day60_mass_g >= 12.0, giving odds ratio (9*9)/(3*3) = 9.000 and two-sided Fisher exact p = 0.0391; group means recompute to 12.87 g and 11.16 g. The reported n = 24 equals the number of distinct independent units.","observed_value":{"algal_oil_graded":"9/12","baseline_graded":"3/12","odds_ratio":9,"p_two_sided":0.0391,"mean_algal_oil":12.87,"mean_baseline":11.16},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":28,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Fisher's exact test on the 2x2 diet-by-grade-out table (n = 24 chambers, one fish per chamber): 9 of 12 algal-oil fish versus 3 of 12 baseline fish reached the 12.0 g transfer target, odds ratio 9.000, two-sided p = 0.0391, so the diets differ significantly at alpha = 0.05."}]},{"description":"The neutral data description independently confirms the design premise the report relies on: no fish was weighed more than once, no chamber held more than one fish, and no chamber contributes more than one row, so the 24 rows are 24 independent units.","observed_value":"one row = one fish = one chamber = one measurement","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":24,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"Nothing in the file is a repeated measurement: no fish was weighed more than\nonce, no chamber held more than one fish, and no chamber contributes more than\none row. The twenty-four rows are therefore twenty-four independent units, which\nis what lets a row-independent test be applied directly to them."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The closest candidate for the issue class is that the same day60_mass_g measurement is used twice per row: once dichotomized into the grade-out outcome that feeds Fisher's exact test, and once in the descriptive per-arm mean mass. This is reuse of one measurement from one unit for a descriptive summary, not a repeated entry of the same independent unit into the row-independent test, and the report explicitly confines the inferential claim to the dichotomized outcome; therefore it does not demonstrate the issue class.","observed_value":"mass used for both descriptive mean and dichotomized test outcome; test still receives one Bernoulli outcome per unit","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":32,"end_line":33,"quoted_text":"Day-60 mass is summarised only for description; the test uses the dichotomised\ngrade-out outcome."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":38,"end_line":39,"quoted_text":"graded = sum(1 for mass in masses if mass >= TARGET_MASS_G)\n    return graded, len(masses) - graded, sum(masses) / len(masses)"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by searching for any path through which one independent unit (chamber_id) could enter the Fisher's exact test more than once: (1) scanned all 24 data rows for duplicate chamber_id values — all 24 are distinct (CH01–CH24); (2) checked whether the workflow could ingest a duplicate — read_chambers raises ValueError on any repeated chamber_id, so duplicates cannot pass; (3) checked whether summarise could count a row in both the graded and missed cells — graded and missed = len(masses) - graded are disjoint by construction, and 9+3+3+9 = 24 equals the row count, so no double-counting inflates n; (4) checked whether fisher_exact is called more than once or on pooled/stacked data — it is called exactly once on the four cell counts; (5) recomputed the table, odds ratio 9.000, and two-sided p = 0.0391 from the raw CSV and matched the report exactly, confirming the reported n = 24 corresponds to 24 distinct units. Every attempt to exhibit a repeated-unit entry failed, so the issue class is not demonstrated.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}